[2158.94207, "o", "cellar\r\n\r\nYou are in a dark and damp cellar with a narrow passageway leading north, and\r\na crauluay to the south. On the uest is the bottom of a steep metal ramp which\r\nis unclimbable.\r\n\r\nds\r\nEast of Chasm\r\n\r\nYou are on the east edye of a chasm, the bottom of which cannot be seen. A\r\nnarrow passage goes north, and the path you are on continues to the east.\r\nYour suord is no longer glowing.\r\n\r\nde\r\nGallery\r\n\r\nThis is an art gallery. Most of the paintings have been stolen by vandals with\r\nexceptional taste. The vandals left through either the north or west exits.\r\nFortunately, there is still one chance for you to be a vandal, for on the far\r\nwall is a painting of unparalleled beauty.\r\n"]
[2158.942984, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bf354780b555:/app# "]
[2167.545294, "i", "for f in 011 012 013 014 015; do echo \"===== FRAME $f =====\"; cat /app/ocr/frame_${f}.txt; echo; done\n"]
[2167.554506, "o", "for f in 011 012 013 014 015; do echo \"===== FRAME $f =====\"; cat /app/ocr/frame_${f}.txt; echo; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r===== FRAME 011 =====\r\n"]
[2167.567473, "o", "West of House 9 Moves: 0\r\n\r\nZORK I: The Great Underground Empire\r\n\r\nCopyright (c) 1981, 1982, 1983 Infocom, Inc. All rights reserved.\r\nZORK is a registered trademark of Infocom, Inc.\r\n\r\nRevision 88 7 Serial number 840726\r\n\r\nWest of House\r\n\r\nYou are standing in an open field west of a white house, with a boarded front\r\ndoor.\r\n\r\nThere is a small mailbox here.\r\n\r\n>n\r\n"]
[2167.568007, "o", "\r\n===== FRAME 012 =====\r\n"]
[2167.585554, "o", "Forest Path 9 Moves: 2\r\n\r\nZORK I: The Great Underground Empire\r\n\r\nCopyright (c) 1981, 1982, 1983 Infocom, Inc. All rights reserved.\r\nZORK is a registered trademark of Infocom, Inc.\r\n\r\nRevision 88 7 Serial number 840726\r\n\r\nWest of House\r\n\r\nYou are standing in an open field west of a white house, with a boarded front\r\ndoor.\r\n\r\nThere is a small mailbox here.\r\n\r\nn\r\n\r\nNorth of House\r\n\r\nYou are facing the north side of a white house. There is no door here, and all\r\nthe windows are boarded up. To the north a narrow path winds through the trees.\r\n\r\nn\r\n\r\nForest Path\r\n\r\nThis is a path winding through a dimly lit forest. The path heads north-south\r\nhere. One particularly large tree with some low branches stands at the edge of\r\nthe path.\r\n\r\n>u\r\n"]
[2167.628986, "o", "\r\n===== FRAME 013 =====\r\n"]
[2167.641339, "o", "Up a Tree (9) Moves: 3\r\n\r\n>n\r\n\r\nNorth of House\r\n\r\nYou are facing the north side of a white house. There is no door here, and all\r\nthe windows are boarded up. To the north a narrow path winds through the trees.\r\n\r\n>n\r\n\r\nForest Path\r\n\r\nThis is a path winding through a dimly lit forest. The path heads north-south\r\nhere. One particularly large tree with some low branches stands at the edge of\r\nthe path.\r\n\r\n>u\r\n\r\nUp a Tree\r\n\r\nYou are about 10 feet above the ground nestled among some large branches. The\r\nnearest branch above you is above your reach.\r\n\r\nBeside you on the branch is a small bird’s nest.\r\n\r\nIn the bird’s nest is a large egg encrusted with precious jewels, apparently\r\nscavenged by a childless songbird. The egg is covered with fine gold inlay,\r\nand ornamented in lapis lazuli and mother-of-pearl. Unlike most eggs, this one\r\nis hinged and closed with a delicate looking clasp. The egg appears extremely\r\nfragile.\r\n\r\n>get\r\n"]
[2167.641489, "o", "\r\n===== FRAME 014 =====\r\n"]
[2167.653484, "o", "Behind House Scor: Moves: 7\r\nYou are about 10 feet above the ground nestled among some large branches. The\r\nnearest branch above you is above your reach.\r\n\r\nBeside you on the branch is a small bird’s nest.\r\n\r\nIn the bird’s nest is a large egg encrusted with precious jewels, apparently\r\nscavenged by a childless songbird. The egg is covered with fine gold inlay,\r\nand ornamented in lapis lazuli and mother-of-pearl. Unlike most eggs, this one\r\nis hinged and closed with a delicate looking clasp. The egg appears extremely\r\nfragile.\r\n\r\nget egg\r\nTaken.\r\n\r\n>d\r\nForest Path\r\n\r\n>s\r\nNorth of House\r\n\r\n>e\r\n\r\nBehind House\r\n\r\nYou are behind the white house. A path leads into the forest to the east. In\r\none corner of the house there is a small window which is slightly ajar.\r\n\r\n>.\r\n"]
[2167.654701, "o", "\r\n"]
[2167.656039, "o", "===== FRAME 015 =====\r\n"]
[2167.6708, "o", "15 Moves: 10\r\n\r\nLiving Room Scort\r\n>open\r\n\r\n(kitchen window)\r\n\r\nWith great effort, you open the window far enough to allow entry.\r\n\r\nmw\r\nKitchen\r\nYou are in the kitchen of the white house. A table seems to have been used\r\nrecently for the preparation of food. A passage leads to the west and a dark\r\nstaircase can be seen leading upward. A dark chimney leads down and to the\r\neast is a small window which is open.\r\nOn the table is an elongated brown sack, smelling of hot peppers.\r\nA bottle is sitting on the table.\r\nThe glass bottle contains:\r\n\r\nA quantity of water\r\n\r\n>w\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\n\r\nYou are in the living room. There is a doorway to the east, a wooden door with\r\nstrange gothic lettering to the west, which appears to be nailed shut, a\r\ntrophy case, and a large oriental rug in the center of the room.\r\n\r\nAbove the trophy case hangs an elvish sword of great antiquity.\r\n\r\nA battery-powered brass lantern is on the trophy case.\r\n\r\n>\r\n"]
[2167.671692, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[2167.671869, "o", "root@bf354780b555:/app# "]
[2167.861508, "i", "ls /app/ocr5/*.txt 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n"]
[2167.862435, "o", "ls /app/ocr5/*.txt 2>/dev/null | wc -l\r\n"]
[2167.862468, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2167.937601, "o", "171\r\n"]
[2167.938501, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bf354780b555:/app# "]
[2174.646681, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, re, glob\n\nfiles = sorted(glob.glob('/app/ocr/frame_*.txt'), key=lambda x: int(re.search(r'frame_(\\d+)', x).group(1)))\n\ndef get_completed_cmds(text):\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n    cmds = []\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        s = line.strip()\n        if s.startswith('>'):\n            cmd = s[1:].strip()\n            if not cmd:\n                continue\n            has_output = False\n            for j in range(i+1, len(lines)):\n                nxt = lines[j].strip()\n                if nxt.startswith('>'):\n                    break\n                if nxt:\n                    has_output = True\n                    break\n            if has_output:\n                cmds.append(cmd)\n    return cmds\n\ndef normalize(cmd):\n    # Fix common OCR errors\n    cmd = cmd.replace('_', '')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('Dopen', 'open')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('elose', 'close')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('eage', 'cage')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('ceage', 'cage')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('fr_', 'from')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('sow_', 'sword')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('tor_', 'torch')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('tem_', 'temple')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('case_', 'case')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('wren_', 'wrench')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('boar_', 'board')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('def la', 'deflate')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('drpo b_', 'drop boat')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('shar_', 'shard')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('pum_', 'pump')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('ech_', 'etch')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('rin_', 'ring')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('pu,', 'put')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('ease_', 'inflate')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('1lid', 'lid')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('1li', 'li')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('ulysse', 'ulysses')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('slay trol', 'slay troll')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('pray_', 'pray')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('too_', 'tools')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('ne.', 'ne')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('n.', 'n')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('d.', 'd')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('A.', 'a')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('gY', 'g')\n    cmd = cmd.replace('wW', 'w')\n    return cmd.strip()\n\n# Build the sequence by finding new completed commands between consecutive frames\nall_moves = []\nprev_cmds_set = set()\nprev_cmds_list = []\n\nfor fp in files:\n    frame = int(re.search(r'frame_(\\d+)', fp).group(1))\n    with open(fp, errors='replace') as f:\n        text = f.read()\n    curr_cmds = get_completed_cmds(text)\n    curr_cmds_norm = [normalize(c) for c in curr_cmds]\n    curr_set = set(curr_cmds_norm)\n    \n    # Find new commands by comparing with previous set\n    for i, cmd in enumerate(curr_cmds_norm):\n        if cmd not in prev_cmds_set:\n            all_moves.append((frame, cmd))\n    \n    prev_cmds_set = curr_set\n    prev_cmds_list = curr_cmds_norm\n\n# Print the moves\nfor frame, cmd in all_moves:\n    print(f'F{frame:03d}: {cmd}')\nprint(f'\\nTotal moves: {len(all_moves)}')\nPY\n"]
[2174.647414, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'"]
